* Mon May 02 2016 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 0.99.2-1BX06
- Modified server/basetypes.schema to update the regexp for 'password' to
  only allow passwords that our architecture actually supports. One problem
  is cce.so not quoting the password, which disallows whitespaces. The other
  issue is storage related (CODB) and transposition to octal values. One
  char it chokes on is ']'. Another issue are chars getting escaped, when they
  should not be escaped. The current regexp from this commit reduces the allowed
  subset of chars to what we can actually support all across the board in all
  usage scenarios. 

* Thu Jan 14 2016 Michael Stauber <mstauber@solarspeed.net> 0.99.2-1BX05
- Rollback to 0.99.2-1BX03 (R:2241 + R:2364 without R:2358) to remove
  memcached functionality. Even if memcached is disabled via the GUI cced
  exhibits various problems on GET requests for valid Objects. Which breaks
  a hell of a lot of things for no apparent reason. We might have a memory
  leak in the CCEd with the memcache functionality. So it needs to go for
  now and will only come back again once all issues are ironed out. Sorry.

